0226da6f727ae53782aae2b0222efff700bf339dd9bd2","file":"preprints/Symplectic-Balls-in-Symmetric-Polar-Products-September-22-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex","line":22,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"11fe8349c58f11cc03fa078b0f3242856c4ebf38affab1ddb3d88d384ab56279","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Symplectic-Balls-in-Symmetric-Polar-Products-September-22-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:c98d680617afecb21ea0226da6f727ae53782aae2b0222efff700bf339dd9bd2","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Symplectic-Balls-in-Symmetric-Polar-Products-September-22-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex#L22"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nFor every integer $n\\ge2$ and every origin-symmetric convex body\n$K\\subset\\R^n$,\n\\[\n c_G(U_K)=4.\n\\]\nMore precisely, for every $0<c<4$ there is a smooth symplectic embedding\n$B^{2n}(c)\\hookrightarrow U_K$."}
